{"type": "thinking", "text": "Patch: Patch specification Total dose / Release rate; Total amount in patch (mg); presets 0.36 mg, 0.72 mg; Count; date/time. No Application/Tablets per dose. Good — so fields are form-specific! So Injection and Gel showing Application Oral/Sublingual and Tablets per dose is inconsistent with Patch which shows patch-specific. Interesting.\n\nWait — patch has \"Total dose\" selected default and \"Total amount in patch (mg)\" with presets 0.36/0.72. Could this be the \"forms with several variants\" — patch spec? Hmm, \"forms with several variants now resolve their sub-type only from an explicit pick\" — Preparation type Ampule/Vial for injection, Container/Sachet for gel, Total dose/Release rate for patch. Those are \"preparation type\" variants. And the note means sub-type resolved only from explicit pick (no default?). But here Injection defaulted to \"Ampule\" checked and gel \"Container\" checked and patch \"Total dose\" checked. That contradicts \"only from an explicit pick\"... unless \"explicit pick\" includes a default when selecting a form? Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the bug is that when changing preparation form with variants, the sub-type (Preparation type) defaults to the first option instead of requiring explicit selection. The note says \"forms with several variants now resolve their sub-type only from an explicit pick\" — expected: selecting a form with several variants should require user to choose the sub-type, i.e., none preselected. Observed: \"Ampule\" auto-checked, \"Container\" auto-checked, \"Total dose\" auto-checked. That would be a bug relative to the changelog intent. But is the note describing the change (fixed behavior)? It says \"Changed in this build: ... Preparation form picker: forms with several variants now resolve their sub-type only from an explicit pick.\" This means the intended behavior is that sub-type is only set from explicit pick. If we see auto-selected sub-type when switching forms, that's a bug.\n\nHmm, but \"Ampule\" appears checked after selecting Injection. Maybe because I previously had something? No — fresh editor, I tapped Injection directly from Tablet. It showed Ampule checked. So it's auto-defaulted. Similarly Gel→Container checked by default. So possibly bug.\n\nBut let me think about what \"resolve their sub-type only from an explicit pick\" might mean in terms of a subtle bug: maybe when switching between forms, the previously chosen Preparation type persisted inappropriately. E.g., if I pick Injection → Vial, then switch to Gel, the Gel's \"Container\" might show checked but internally still Vial? Then saving would record wrong subtype. That's the kind of bug to test: \"resolve sub-type only from an explicit pick\" = when a form has multiple variants, the sub-type shouldn't be inferred from stale state; only explicit pick should set it.\n\nLet me test carefully. Since we have no existing medicines, adding one via this sheet will create a medication record (log). The \"Medicines list\" must be somewhere else — maybe Settings or the Journal? Let me explore after adding.\n\nActually, let's first test saving a medicine and then examine the medication card and Medicines list. But I want to check form switching stale subtype issue.\n\nTest plan:\n1. Open editor → Tablet defaults.\n2. Select Injection → note sub-type Ampule auto-checked.\n3. Select Vial explicitly.\n4. Switch to Gel → is \"Container\" checked, or is Vial leaking (no visible category)? If Container checked, then no leak. Switch back to Injection → does it show Ampule or Vial? If it shows Ampule (reset) vs Vial (remembered) — either could be acceptable. The bug would be if a form inherits another form's subtype.\n\nActually the \"sub-type only from an explicit pick\" likely means: when user selects a preparation form, if it has variants, the app shouldn't auto-pick a variant; the user must pick one. The default checkmark on Ampule contradicts that. Let's test by choosing Injection and immediately saving — see what gets recorded (maybe it records null subtype or Ampule). If it records Ampule without explicit pick, that's a bug against the stated change.\n\nLet me gather more evidence. Also there's the missing strength field for Injection: compare GnRHa injection has \"Strength per injection (mg)\". Estradiol injection has no strength field at all, just Application/Tablets per dose. That seems like a big bug: cannot record injection dose.\n\nHold on — maybe the Estradiol Injection form is supposed to display a strength field, but because the sub-type wasn't explicitly selected, the strength field is missing. \"forms with several variants now resolve their sub-type only from an explicit pick\" — perhaps the strength field depends on variant (Ampule vs Vial have different preset strengths); since no explicit pick... but Ampule is checked. Hmm.\n\nLet me try tapping \"Vial\" and see if fields change (maybe strength appears)."}
