e tablet fields (Application Oral/Sublingual, Tablets per dose) instead of injection strength; only after explicitly tapping a sub-type does injection-specific fields appear. (symptom: wrong_value/no_effect? probably \"no_effect\" or \"wrong_value\"). Expected: either no sub-type preselected and user prompted, or Ampule selected resolves Ampule-specific fields.\n2. Ampule strength label says \"Vial strength (mg)\". (wrong_value)\n\nLet me continue exploring, but first maybe let's save some records to test the medicines list/cards. The editor might auto-save on Save. Let me cancel and do a proper flow with Tablet to create a medicine, then check the list. Actually to test medication cards and lists, we need medicines. Let's save one.\n\nBut careful: \"Do not change data outside what testing requires.\" Adding medicines is required. Fine.\n\nLet me now check Gel with explicit sub-type too (Container auto-checked vs Sachet). Let me test later.\n\nFirst, let me establish the Ampule label issue in a clean run. Cancel now."}
