{"type": "thinking", "text": "Medicines list works with one item. The header \"ESTRADIOL\" is category, item \"Estradiol valerate / Tablet · 2 mg\".\n\nNow, the changed area \"Medicines list header: the header is now built from the same data source as the list below.\" We need to test with multiple categories to see headers grouping correctly. Add medicines from different categories (Antiandrogen, Custom) and check grouping headers. Also test empty state after deleting all? Reversal.\n\nAlso \"medication cards and lists\" — the card on Home/Plan shows dosing subtitle.\n\nLet me test the fraction formatting on cards by editing the existing record's tablets-per-dose to 1/3, 1/8 etc. Actually the \"dosing subtitle\" is derived from the medicine details + record? The card shows \"Oral · 1/2 tablets · 1 mg\". The medicine list shows \"Tablet · 2 mg\". So the card's subtitle uses a fraction for tablets per dose. The medicine's \"Tablet · 2 mg\" doesn't include the fraction. Hmm. So the fraction formatting shows on medication cards (Home/Plan). We saw \"1/2 tablets\". Potential issues:\n- Plural \"tablets\" with fraction 1/2. Usually grammar would be \"0.5 tablet\". But maybe design intent uses \"tablets\" always? The changelog says \"pill fractions are now formatted through a single general rule\". A single general rule likely converts 0.5 -> \"1/2\" and 0.25 -> \"1/4\", 0.333 -> \"1/3\"? And maybe 0.75 -> \"3/4\" — but the editor only offers 1/8, 1/4, 1/3, 1/2, 1. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the \"Tablets per dose\" seekbar allows continuous values; the dots are just markers but tapping interpolates to nearest? The SeekBar steps might be 0.125 increments with 5 dots at 1/8,1/4,1/3(?),1/2,1. Odd.\n\nActually maybe the seekbar has 5 discrete presets: 1/8, 1/4, 1/3, 1/2, 1. Why 1/3? Odd. Could be 0.125, 0.25, 0.333, 0.5, 1.0. Hmm, these could be \"1/8, 1/4, 1/3, 1/2, 1\" as common pill fractions. Interesting.\n\nPotential formatting bug: 1/3 may be displayed as \"0.33333334 tablets\" on the card if not handled by general rule. Let's test editing record to 1/3 and see card.\n\nThe edit record button (pencil) on Home card. But maybe easier: edit the medicine? The medicine details \"Tablet · 2 mg\" only show strength. The card subtitle is per record.\n\nLet me go back to Plan (or Home) and edit the record. Tap back to Plan; then tap the record maybe opens log detail, but \"Edit record\" button in Home. Let me use Home.\n\nFirst, let's inspect Medicine list item click behavior — tapping opens medicine detail/editor. Let's tap the item to see."}
