{"type": "thinking", "text": "Cards updated to EV 2mg. Persistence good.\n\nNow test the doctor's note about \"Category picker in the medicine editor: categories are now taken from one shared catalogue.\" Perhaps a bug where the category picker in the record editor (Home pencil → Add medicine) shows different categories from the one in the Medicines list editor. We already saw both: same categories. Also the category order: Estradiol, Antiandrogen, SERM, GnRHa, Custom. Identical.\n\nBut maybe there's a subtle bug: In the record editor \"Add medicine\", after you add a medicine, the category picker... Hmm.\n\nMaybe the shared catalogue bug: The category selected in the \"Add medicine\" editor may not be saved correctly (e.g., choose Antiandrogen but the medicine is stored under ESTRADIOL header). We tested: Spironolactone showed under ANTIANDROGEN. Good. Test SERM or GnRHa similarly? Could be a mapping bug only for some categories. Let's test Custom (Testosterone showed CUSTOM, correct). Test GnRHa (Triptorelin) and SERM (Raloxifene) maybe. We can add these medicines and check the list grouping. That's within scope.\n\nBut adding many medicines clutters. Still, test the category header. Let's add a GnRHa medicine. Also this tests the injection preparation form within GnRHa (Triptorelin) - it's injection-only, strength per injection, no variants maybe.\n\nLet's do from Medicines list Add medicine. But we're on Plan. Tap Medicines, Add medicine, GnRHa. Then select strength 3.75, save. Check list shows GNRHA header. Do it."}
