{"type": "thinking", "text": "New card (element 19): \"Oral · 2 mg\" — no tablets per dose shown! With Count=2 and per-dose 1/2, the subtitle shows \"Oral · 2 mg\". Hmm. Wait: 1/2 tablet × 2 count = 1 tablet → 2 mg total. So the card collapses to total dose \"2 mg\" and omits the \"1/2 tablets\" part. Is that expected? The card for count 1 shows \"Oral · 1/2 tablets · 1 mg\". For count 2 it shows \"Oral · 2 mg\" (no fraction). Hmm, maybe the subtitle is designed to show the total tablets only when count>1? But it shows no tablet count at all. That seems inconsistent: the card should probably show \"1/2 tablets × 2\" or \"1 tablet\" or \"2 mg\". \n\nWait, maybe the card's subtitle is \"Oral · 2 mg\" because 2 doses of 1/2 tablet = 1 tablet = 2 mg, and the app only shows the total mg. But for count=1 it shows \"1/2 tablets · 1 mg\". Why omit per-dose for count=2? That inconsistency could be a bug in the dosing subtitle (the changed area!). Specifically, the \"dosing subtitle\" should probably show the fraction regardless of count, or show count. Let me verify this is a record card for the new record (6th). The last card is \"Oral · 2 mg\". The time is 1:18 PM. So yes.\n\nHmm, wait: maybe the count field is not \"number of doses\" but \"number of tablets\"? In the editor, \"Count\" = 2 and \"Tablets per dose\" = 1/2. The dose total could be 1 tablet. If Count is actually the number of tablets to take, then \"Tablets per dose\" is redundant/confusing. But the card's \"2 mg\" suggests 1 tablet = 2 mg (since count 2 × 1/2 = 1). So it computed total.\n\nIs \"Oral · 2 mg\" acceptable? For a medication card, showing total dose is okay. But inconsistent with count=1, which shows \"1/2 tablets · 1 mg\". If the general rule is to always show per-dose fraction, count=2 should show \"1/2 tablets × 2 · 2 mg\" or \"1 tablet · 2 mg\". Missing tablets info is a \"missing\" defect. But is this in the changed area? \"Dosing subtitle on medication cards: pill fractions are now formatted through a single general rule.\" The subtitle with count=2 loses the fraction entirely, so it's relevant.\n\nLet me check the Plan list card for the same record; maybe the Plan row shows same. It will. Let me double check the record detail \"Edit record\" summary shows \"Oral · 2 mg\". Hmm.\n\nBut maybe the design is: when count > 1, show total mg only, because per-dose fraction × count isn't a simple fraction. That could be intentional. Hard to call a bug.\n\nAnother thing: the record card at [19] shows only \"Oral · 2 mg\" without a \"MANUAL\" or time? The element description lacks time because the card's content maybe \"Oral · 2 mg\". On Home, the card rows don't show time (the grouping bar shows the time range). The Plan list shows time \"1:18 PM\". Fine.\n\nLet me not over-report. The \"1 tablets\" is logged; the count=2 case might be acceptable.\n\nLet's now test a Gel medicine to see if the unresolved subtype bug also affects the saved record (or if explicit pick yields correct forms). This is part of \"adding medicines and choosing preparation form\". Add Gel via Medicines list. We'll select Container → explicitly tap Sachet or Container. If we leave default Container, Save does nothing (observed). That's already part of bug 1. If we explicitly pick Sachet, fill concentration and amount, save, then see list subtitle. Let's do it to test that the form persists correctly. Use Medicines list Add medicine → Gel → Sachet → 0.1% → 1.0g → save. Then check list item shows \"Gel · Sachet · 0.1% · 1.0g\" or similar.\n\nBut first, current Home. Go Plan → Medicines → Add medicine."}
