{"type": "thinking", "text": "All good. The Medicines list is long now. Does it scroll? The Add medicine button is at 1785, visible. Fine.\n\nNow, I should test the \"Medicines list header\" behavior when scrolling or when the same medicine appears twice under same category. It groups properly. Good.\n\nPotential issue: The medicine list header \"ESTRADIOL\" and items sorted; no bug.\n\nNow, the major confirmed bug is the prep form subtype default. We also have the \"1 tablets\" bug logged.\n\nOther possible bugs in the changed areas:\n- The \"pill fractions\" general rule: maybe fractions on the *medicine editor* strength or elsewhere? Let's check the \"dosing subtitle\" for 1/3, 1/8, 1/2 and 1. We tested. The \"1/2 tablets\" plural. Is that a bug? The single general rule likely intended to format 0.5 as \"1/2\", etc. The unit pluralization could be handled by the rule. Since \"1 tablets\" is confirmed, maybe also \"1/2 tablets\" should be \"1/2 tablet\". But the developer confirmed only \"1 tablets\"; the fix may also adjust fractions. Fine.\n\n- Maybe there is a bug where count=2 drops the fraction; but not sure.\n\n- Category picker: shared catalogue. Could there be a mismatch between the categories in the \"Add medicine\" from Medicines list vs from the \"Add manual record\" flow? We saw identical. Good.\n\n- Prep form picker: aside from unresolved default, check that when switching categories, prep form selection resets to a valid form. E.g., Estradiol → Gel → switch to Antiandrogen. Does it reset to Tablet? Let's test; if it keeps \"Gel\" (invalid), that's a bug. Earlier I tapped Gel then... I didn't switch category. Let me test now quickly (from Add medicine without saving). Tap Add medicine → Gel → Antiandrogen. Observe prep form options and whether Gel remains selected/invalid.\n\nLet's do."}
