{"type": "thinking", "text": "Switching category resets form to Tablet. Good.\n\nNow switch from Antiandrogen/Tablet to GnRHa: form should become Injection. Then to SERM: Tablet. Already seen earlier. Fine.\n\nTest \"Injection\" selected under Antiandrogen doesn't exist (only Tablet/Capsule), good.\n\nPotential issue: switching category and back to Estradiol resets the prep form to Tablet, losing user's form choice; that's expected.\n\nNow, the explicit sub-type pick for Injection and Gel: We found the initial default not resolved. The bug is logged. Let me also test what happens if a user picks \"Gel\" then \"Container\" (already checked) — tapping the checked Container may not change anything and no fields appear. So the user might tap Container (thinking to select it) and nothing happens, then Save does nothing. That's the worst UX. Our bug report covers it. Good.\n\nNow let's test the \"1 tablets\" bug more: Is it also in the record editor summary \"Oral · 1 tablets · 2 mg\"? Yes, edit record sheet shows same summary. So consistent wrong grammar. Fine.\n\nNow maybe there's a bug with the count=2 subtitle missing fractions. Let me consider whether to report. The card shows \"Oral · 2 mg\" for a record with 1/2 tablet × 2. The user loses the important \"how many pills\" info (1/2 per dose ×2). But the app may intentionally show total amount. Hmm. Since the changed area is \"dosing subtitle ... pill fractions formatted through a single general rule\", a card with count 2 not showing fraction may be by design (since total tablets = 1, i.e., fraction resolved to whole). Actually 1/2 × 2 = 1 tablet, so it could legitimately display \"1 tablet · 2 mg\". Instead it shows \"2 mg\" with no tablets. That's a \"missing\" tablets count, but the dose mg is correct.\n\nWait, maybe the \"Count\" field is the number of *tablets* taken, and \"Tablets per dose\" is the strength fraction? Hmm. Let's reason: For the first record, \"tablets per dose\" 1/2, count 1 → subtitle \"1/2 tablets · 1 mg\". For count 2, subtitle \"2 mg\" only. If count meant number of tablets, then 2 × 1/2 tablet = 1 tablet? No. If count means number of doses, total = 1 tablet = 2 mg. The subtitle \"2 mg\" accounts for total mg but drops \"1 tablet\". Maybe intentional to avoid \"1/2 tablets × 2\". I won't report.\n\nLet's look at the Add record editor's \"Count\" stepper: Count label with # icon and +/-; max? Could be 10? Not important.\n\nNext, test the \"Edit record\" flow for the count=2 record: the summary displays \"Oral · 2 mg\". If we change date/time and save, is the dose retained? We can test persistence of the record after editing date/time. Not changed area though.\n\nNow, the Medicines list header built from the same data source. Maybe there's a subtle bug when a medicine's category is changed via edit? Edit medicine doesn't allow category change (only name/strength). Fine.\n\nWhat about archiving a medicine that has records? The dialog says history kept. Header should drop it from list. We archived Testosterone custom earlier; header disappeared. Good.\n\nNow test the \"Medicines\" list empty state reversal: archive all custom? We have several. Not necessary.\n\nLet's run through the remaining checklist items:\n- State: Leave and come back (we did many times) — data persists.\n- Reversal: Cancel archive (tested), cancel edit sheet (tested), cancel add medicine (tested). Undo changes? The seekbar changes cancel with Cancel; tested implicitly when dismissing sheet? We cancelled after changing things (Gel) and data not saved. We could verify that cancelled new medicine didn't appear. Yes after cancel of earlier gel attempt, list had no gel until we saved. Good.\n- Repetition: We added multiple records same medicine; works. Archive cancel repeated.\n- Input: empty name/strength validation works. Unusual values: Custom μg unit, decimal strength? Test unit μg and decimal 0.5? Possibly interesting: selecting μg and entering a decimal; check list subtitle. But not changed area.\n- Consistency: Cards update after rename; medicine list matches details; card subtitles match record values.\n- Device: rotation — Home content survived; but what about a bottom sheet open during rotation? Could lose input. The instruction says rotate and check nothing is lost. Let's test rotating with the Add medicine sheet open and values entered, see if the sheet/fields persist. This could be a bug (bottom sheet dismissed on rotation or values lost). But it may be out of changed areas; still \"device\" testing. Let's test quickly: we're in Add medicine with Antiandrogen selected. Rotate to landscape and back. See if the editor stays and values persist. Since it's an unsaved editor, maybe rotate dismisses. But it's worth testing within the sweep.\n\nActually, be careful: if rotation dismisses the sheet, we'd see it as data loss. But many apps recreate the activity and the bottom sheet state is lost — could be a legitimate bug but not in changed areas. Still part of \"adding medicines\".\n\nLet me first type a name/strength, then rotate. Current screen Antiandrogen with empty strength. Let's set 50 mg then rotate landscape. Actually let me just rotate now and observe."}
