{"type": "thinking", "text": "Gel card subtitle: \"Gel · 0.1% · 1 g\". No count shown, but count=1 so okay. It's consistent with medicine list \"Gel · Sachet · 0.1% · 1 g\" minus \"Sachet\". Fine.\n\nNow, Home with 7 records and scroll; all visible when scrolled.\n\nTesting is getting extensive. Let's consider remaining changed-area checks:\n\nA) \"Medicines list header: the header is now built from the same data source as the list below.\" Test more: Does the header update immediately after adding a medicine? Yes. After archiving the only item category, header disappears. Yes. Maybe test deleting a medicine with records? Archive doesn't delete. Fine.\n\nB) \"Dosing subtitle on medication cards: pill fractions are now formatted through a single general rule.\" We found \"1 tablets\". Any other formatting? Let's inspect the fraction formatting with a different strength to see rounding: e.g., 1/3 of 1 mg = 0.33 mg; 1/8 of 1 mg = 0.13 mg (rounding). Not a bug likely. Maybe the general rule produces \"1/3\" but if the underlying value stored is 0.333333, the card's computed dose uses 0.3333 → 0.6667 → 0.67. Fine.\n\nCould there be an inconsistency between the editor's fraction label and the card's? Editor \"1/3\", card \"1/3\" — consistent.\n\nC) \"Category picker in the medicine editor: categories are now taken from one shared catalogue.\" We tested all categories and headers. Could test that the \"Add record\" screen list (which lists medicines grouped by category) uses the same category names (ESTRADIOL, ANTIANDROGEN, SERM, GNRHA). It does. Good.\n\nD) \"Preparation form picker: forms with several variants now resolve their sub-type only from an explicit pick.\" Found the main bug. We reported it. The dev confirmed and logged. Maybe there are more related bugs:\n- When switching from Injection (Ampule) to Gel (Container), the fields are missing; already in bug 1.\n- The Ampule label \"Vial strength (mg)\" — dev couldn't reproduce. Maybe it's a real bug but rejected; could be the same root cause as bug 1 and the fix will address it? Hmm, but the dev confirmed bug 1, maybe the fix will also fix the label.\n- When explicit subtype is selected and then user switches to another *category* where the form is not available, does subtype reset? We saw category switch resets form. Good.\n- When explicit subtype is selected and user switches to a category that supports the same form (Estradiol Injection → GnRHa Injection), are the subtype options appropriate? Injections in Estradiol have Ampule/Vial, GnRHa injection has no subtypes. Does the GnRHa form show no prep type? Yes: earlier GnRHa showed Injection only, no Preparation type. Good.\n\nLet me verify that after explicitly selecting Injection/Ampule in Estradiol, then switching category to GnRHa, the fields are GnRHa strength per injection and not stale Ampule. We can test: Add medicine → Estradiol → Injection → Vial → then category GnRHa. The form options for GnRHa only Injection, selected. Does it show \"Strength per injection (mg)\" with Triptorelin? Let's test. This is a good consistency check for the prep form picker (sub-type resolution when category changes). If stale Vial fields persist, bug.\n\nLet's do: Add medicine → Injection → Vial → GnRHa. Current screen after saving gel is Home. Go Plan → Medicines → Add medicine. But we're now Home scrolled; use element 28 pencil? Actually the top app bar pencil is element 28. Plan > Medicines. Let me use Plan bottom nav (31) then Medicines.\n\nWait, on Home the element 31 is Plan? [31] Plan @(417,2189). Yes.\n\nLet's go."}
