{"type": "thinking", "text": "Interesting: I set the display name to a single space and saved; the medicine details still shows \"Estradiol\"! So the edit either was rejected silently or it trimmed whitespace and kept the old name. The details show \"Gel | Estradiol | Gel · Container...\" — name \"Estradiol\" unchanged. So the empty/whitespace name was rejected (no error message though). Maybe it saved the old name? It didn't change. Not a bug (validation silently prevented empty). The lack of error is minor.\n\nBut wait, if the display name field was \" \" and Save succeeded, the name would be blank or \" \". Instead it's \"Estradiol\". So the app likely ignored/trimmed and did not update. Fine.\n\nWe've done a lot. Let's consider whether to sign off now. Before that, maybe the \"Add medicine\" screen does not indicate required fields until save (fine). The prep subtype bug is the main one.\n\nGiven the session instructions, I should call sign_off when I believe the areas have no remaining bugs. But we know there are logged bugs in the build. The phrase \"no remaining bugs\" after reporting might be impossible until fixed, but the session is designed so we report and then sign off once we've swept. The developer replies \"confirmed and logged. Keep testing the current build.\" So we should continue testing and then sign off. Remaining unreported defects? Let's think:\n\n- \"1/2 tablets\" plural is arguably part of the \"1 tablets\" report (same general rule), so covered.\n- \"Remove patch\" pseudo-medicine in list: could be intended.\n- Save button near nav: minor, and scrollable.\n\nMaybe test the *preparation form picker* on the **Edit medicine** screen: For a medicine with no records, editing a Tablet medicine can change the preparation form? The Edit medicine sheet for the gel/patch shows only display name + variant fields, no \"Preparation form\" picker. So you can't change the form after creation. That's a design choice.\n\nWhat about adding a medicine from the record flow: The editor's title is \"Add record\" (not \"Add medicine\") even when creating a new medicine, and it includes date/time. We did that. Fine.\n\nMaybe there is a bug: When adding a medicine via the \"Add record\" flow, the **medicines list** header shows the new medicine under the category; we saw EV 2mg under ESTRADIOL. Good.\n\nWhat about the \"Add record\" flow's \"Add medicine\" button when medicines exist: At the bottom of the Add manual record list, \"Add medicine\" still exists. Tapping it likely opens the Add medicine sheet. Fine.\n\nLet's test adding a *second* medicine under the same category via the record flow to see if the list header combines; yes, EV 2mg and injection both under ESTRADIOL.\n\nI think we're good.\n\nWait, there's one more thing from the task: \"Device: rotate the screen, and check that nothing is lost.\" We rotated on Home and in the Add medicine sheet. But we didn't check a rotation *while a record editor sheet with values is open* — the values might be lost. Let's test quickly with the record editor: open Home pencil → EV 2mg → set Sublingual + 1/3 + count 2, rotate landscape, rotate back, check values persist. This is a quick but valuable state test. If values are lost, that's a bug in \"adding medicines/records\". Let's do it.\n\nCurrent screen: Medicine details (gel). Go back twice to Plan, Home, pencil. Then choose EV 2mg, set values, rotate.\n\nActually, rotation with a modal sheet open already retained category/form in the Add medicine sheet. The record editor likely retains. But test anyway? It's a few steps. Let's do it quickly.\n\nGo BACK to list, BACK to Plan, Home, pencil."}
