er.\n   - Add medicine validation.\n   - Empty state initial \"No medicines yet\" in Add record; after adding, list shows.\n   - More options \"Stock tracking tips\".\n\nAre there other bugs in these areas that I haven't discovered? Maybe the \"Remove patch\" item should not be in the Medicines list but it's likely intentional.\n\nI could test the `Medicines` list header when a category has only archived items: we archived Testosterone (Custom) and the header disappeared. Good.\n\nWhat about the \"Add manual record\" list header when a category has only archived items: It should not show the header. The Triptorelin is not archived. Fine.\n\nPotential bug: When a medicine is archived while it has records, its records remain (by design \"Logged history will be kept\"), and the card/list still shows the name (from the medicine snapshot). Fine.\n\nMaybe test archive of a medicine with records: EV 2mg has records. Archiving it would keep history; the Medicines list header ESTRADIOL still has other items. The record cards should still show \"EV 2mg\". Could reveal a bug where archived medicine's records break. But that's not in the changed areas, and destructive. We already archived Testosterone with no records. I'll skip.\n\nGiven the thoroughness, I'll sign off. But wait: the instruction \"When you believe the areas above have no remaining bugs, sign off.\" We have *confirmed logged bugs* which are remaining in the build (not fixed). But the workflow expects us to keep testing until no *new* bugs. The developer's replies indicate they log confirmed bugs; no new build installed. Sign-off likely means \"no more bugs to report\". So yes.\n\nHowever, I'm uneasy about the Ampule label bug. Let me think about whether to include it in the sign-off notes as unconfirmed/rejected. The sign_off notes can mention tested areas and that one report was rejected. But the verdict is PASS. If I sign off with a known (but rejected) bug, that contradicts \"no remaining bugs.\" Since the de